            "review_text": "Roving52054624968\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam7 contributions\n0\nTaiwan Mazesoba is rich in flavor and highly recommended in District 1\nAug 2026 • Friends\nThis is the first time I've tried Taiwan Mazesoba at Menya Hanabi and I quite like it. Thick, moderately chewy noodles, rich sauce, when mixed with minced meat, egg yolk, and toppings, are very addictive. The cafe space has a Japanese style, neat, and comfortable. Being close to the office, it's also quite convenient to have lunch or dinner right in District 1 after work. Next time I will come back to try other ramen dishes. I also recommend the karaage fried chicken here, it's very delicious.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten September 8, 2026",
