            "review_text": "Road21509728937\n5 contributions\n0\nA must-try noodle restaurant in Ho Chi Minh City\nAug 2026 • Business\nI visited with a coworker on a weekday evening.\nThe restaurant is right in the center of District 1, within walking distance of Le Thanh Ton and Thai Van Lung.\nThe mazesoba was incredibly rich and hearty — the kind of flavor you can't forget once you've tried it. They take real pride in using sauce imported from Japan, which made experiencing the authentic taste even more appealing.\nI found this place by searching \"ramen,\" but ended up discovering an unusual mazesoba on the menu and decided to order it — it turned out to be a fantastic choice. I'd highly recommend anyone in Ho Chi Minh City give it a try at least once.\nThe finishing \"oimeshi\" (rice added to the leftover sauce) wasn't too heavy either, so I enjoyed every last bite.\nI'd love to come back again.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nSuitable for both solo diners and groups, and alcoholic drinks are also available. In addition to mazesoba and ramen, be sure to try side di\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 8, 2026",
